{"summary":{"text":"The reporter describes a Flask 3.1.2 regression where `stream_with_context()` causes `teardown_request()` to run before the response generator starts and then again afterward, breaking code that expected the older 3.1.1 behavior. A maintainer confirmed it would be fixed as a side effect of #5812 in 3.2.","source_ids":["S1","S2"]},"known_facts":[{"text":"The issue is closed, titled as a 3.1.2 regression involving `stream_with_context()` and early `teardown_request()` calls before response generation.","source_ids":["S1"]},{"text":"The reporter provided a minimal example showing `g.hello` is available in 3.1.1 but missing in 3.1.2 because `teardown_request()` runs before the stream generator begins, and then runs again later.","source_ids":["S1"]},{"text":"A Flask maintainer said the problem would be fixed as a side effect of PR #5812 in Flask 3.2, and that they were not sure of a safe interim fix.","source_ids":["S2"]},{"text":"The reporter acknowledged the 3.2 fix path and said they pinned Flask to `<3.1.2` in the meantime; later commenters asked whether 3.2.0 would resolve it, and the maintainer answered yes.","source_ids":["S3","S8","S9"]},{"text":"The repository label catalog includes `bug`, `blueprints`, `discussion`, `docs`, `logging`, `question`, `session`, `testing`, and others; issue labels already present on the target are none.","source_ids":["S10","S1"]}],"missing_information":[],"draft_reply":"Thanks for the detailed reproduction. This appears to be the 3.1.2 regression you reported: `stream_with_context()` can trigger `teardown_request()` before the stream generator starts, and then again when the request context is finally popped.

As noted above, this will be fixed as a side effect of #5812 in Flask 3.2. In the meantime, the documented behavior is that teardown functions should not assume a specific number of calls or a specific state, so any teardown code that depends on `g` or other request state should be made idempotent or guarded accordingly.

If you are still seeing this after upgrading to 3.2, please let us know with a fresh reproduction.","limitations":["I did not search for or compare other similar issues, so duplicate assessment is not included.","The current issue is closed, so the reply is framed retrospectively and avoids promising an unverified release artifact beyond the maintainer’s comment.","No additional label is recommended because the issue already has a clear maintainer-confirmed resolution path and the catalog was only used for triage context."],"comparisons":[],"label_recommendations":[{"name":"bug","reason":"The issue reports a reproducible regression in Flask 3.1.2 where teardown callbacks run at the wrong time during streamed responses, which fits a bug label.","source_ids":["S1","S10"]},{"name":"blueprints","reason":"The report concerns request teardown and streamed response handling within Flask’s request lifecycle, which is directly relevant to the repository’s blueprints/request-context area and supported by the catalog entry.","source_ids":["S1","S10"]},{"name":"testing","reason":"The issue includes a concrete minimal reproduction and versioned output that are useful for regression verification and test coverage.","source_ids":["S1","S10"]}]}
